#ASSERT `the credit points under section 35 for` (`fid oleh all year in` 2022 `fid who arrived on` (YMD 2021 7 10)) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `fid s35 helper sum for` (`fid oleh all year in` 2022 `fid who arrived on` (YMD 2021 7 10)) EQUALS 3  -- (helper)
-- D049: 2023, months 19-30: 2.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 35 for` (`fid oleh all year in` 2023 `fid who arrived on` (YMD 2021 7 10)) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `fid s35 helper sum for` (`fid oleh all year in` 2023 `fid who arrived on` (YMD 2021 7 10)) EQUALS 2  -- (helper)
-- D050: 2024, months 31-42: 1.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 35 for` (`fid oleh all year in` 2024 `fid who arrived on` (YMD 2021 7 10)) EQUALS 1
-- D051: 2025: 0.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 35 for` (`fid oleh all year in` 2025 `fid who arrived on` (YMD 2021 7 10)) EQUALS 0
-- D052: aliyah 2022-01-01, 2022: 1 (new regime).
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 35 for` (`fid oleh all year in` 2022 `fid who arrived on` (YMD 2022 1 1)) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `fid s35 helper sum for` (`fid oleh all year in` 2022 `fid who arrived on` (YMD 2022 1 1)) EQUALS 1  -- (helper)
-- D053: aliyah 2021-12-31: 2021 (month 1) 0.25; 2022 (months 2-13) 3 (old regime).
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 35 for` (`fid oleh in` 2021 `fid since` (YMD 2021 12 31) `fid resident in months` (LIST 12) `fid first time` TRUE `fid 35(e) rules` FALSE) EQUALS 0.25
#ASSERT `fid s35 helper sum for` (`fid oleh in` 2021 `fid since` (YMD 2021 12 31) `fid resident in months` (LIST 12) `fid first time` TRUE `fid 35(e) rules` FALSE) EQUALS 0.25  -- (helper)
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 35 for` (`fid oleh all year in` 2022 `fid who arrived on` (YMD 2021 12 31)) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `fid s35 helper sum for` (`fid oleh all year in` 2022 `fid who arrived on` (YMD 2021 12 31)) EQUALS 3  -- (helper)
-- D054: aliyah 2026-01-20, 2026: 1.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 35 for` (`fid oleh all year in` 2026 `fid who arrived on` (YMD 2026 1 20)) EQUALS 1
-- D055: second aliyah: refuse (the 1977 rules under (e)(1) are for former immigrants). The scenario
-- says nothing about those rules, so the encoding's input "rules under (e) apply" is given both ways.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 35 for` (`fid oleh in` 2026 `fid since` (YMD 2026 1 20) `fid resident in months` `fid all months` `fid first time` FALSE `fid 35(e) rules` FALSE)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 35 for` (`fid oleh in` 2026 `fid since` (YMD 2026 1 20) `fid resident in months` `fid all months` `fid first time` FALSE `fid 35(e) rules` TRUE)

GIVEN `the ground` IS A `The ground on which a person claims to be an immigrant, for section 35`
      `cancelled`  IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `An immigrant in a tax year, for section 35`
`fid claimant on` `the ground` `fid citizenship cancelled` `cancelled` MEANS
    `An immigrant in a tax year, for section 35` WITH
        `tax year`                                                        IS 2026
        `ground`                                                          IS `the ground`
        `citizenship cancelled under section 10(d) of the Citizenship Law` IS `cancelled`
        `the day the individual became an immigrant`                      IS YMD 2026 1 1
        `the first time the individual became an immigrant`               IS TRUE
        `absence left out of the count at the immigrant's request`        IS NOTHING
        `months of the tax year in which the immigrant resided in Israel` IS `fid all months`
        `rules under section 35(e) apply to the immigrant`                IS FALSE
        `a foreign worker`                                                IS FALSE

