#ASSERT `s 35(b) — the points counted in the registered spouse's calculation, for an immigrant spouse with points` 3 `, section 38 points` 1.75 `, at a credit-point value of` `fid credit point value` `, and income` 60000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 35(b) — the points counted in the registered spouse's calculation, for an immigrant spouse with points` 3 `, section 38 points` 1.75 `, at a credit-point value of` `fid credit point value` `, and income` 68970 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 35(b) — the points counted in the registered spouse's calculation, for an immigrant spouse with points` 3 `, section 38 points` 1.75 `, at a credit-point value of` `fid credit point value` `, and income` 68971 EQUALS 3

§§ `D-F. Sections 37, 38 and 39`

-- One individual, every s 37-39 fact a parameter.
GIVEN `resident`      IS A BOOLEAN
      `spouse`        IS A BOOLEAN
      `self retired`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `spouse retired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `self blind`    IS A BOOLEAN
      `maintenance`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `registered`    IS A BOOLEAN
      `includes`      IS A BOOLEAN
      `exertion`      IS A BOOLEAN
      `spouse income` IS A NUMBER
      `allowance`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `helped`        IS A BOOLEAN
      `elects 39`     IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 37 to 39`
`fid spouse case: resident` `resident` `fid has spouse` `spouse` `fid self retired` `self retired` `fid spouse retired` `spouse retired` `fid self blind` `self blind` `fid maintenance proved` `maintenance` `fid registered` `registered` `fid includes spouse income` `includes` `fid exertion proved` `exertion` `fid spouse income` `spouse income` `fid allowance points` `allowance` `fid spouse helped` `helped` `fid elects 39` `elects 39` MEANS
    `An individual in a tax year, for sections 37 to 39` WITH
        `tax year`                                                                    IS 2026
        `an Israeli resident in the tax year`                                         IS `resident`
        `has a spouse`                                                                IS `spouse`
        `the individual has reached retirement age`                                   IS `self retired`
        `the spouse has reached retirement age`                                       IS `spouse retired`
        `the individual is blind or disabled within section 9(5)(a) or (a1)`         IS `self blind`
        `the spouse is blind or disabled within section 9(5)(a) or (a1)`             IS FALSE
        `proved to the assessing officer's satisfaction that the spouse's maintenance was on the individual in the tax year` IS `maintenance`
        `the registered spouse`                                                       IS `registered`
        `the taxable income includes the spouse's income`                             IS `includes`
        `proved that the spouse's income was from personal exertion within paragraphs (1) to (6) of its definition` IS `exertion`
        `the spouse's taxable income`                                                 IS `spouse income`
        `entitled to allowance points under section 40(a)`                            IS `allowance`
        `the spouse helped at least 24 hours a week, within 9 months of the tax year, in earning the individual's income from a business or profession` IS `helped`
        `the election under section 39 between sections 38 and 39`                    IS (IF `elects 39` THEN `elected the credits of section 39` ELSE `elected the credits of section 38`)
        `a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen`                        IS FALSE
        `a foreign worker`                                                            IS FALSE

-- s 37: (resident, spouse, self retired, spouse retired, self blind, maintenance proved)
GIVEN `resident` IS A BOOLEAN
      `spouse`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `sr`       IS A BOOLEAN
      `pr`       IS A BOOLEAN
      `sb`       IS A BOOLEAN
      `mp`       IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 37 to 39`
`fid s37 case` `resident` `spouse` `sr` `pr` `sb` `mp` MEANS
    `fid spouse case: resident` `resident` `fid has spouse` `spouse` `fid self retired` `sr` `fid spouse retired` `pr` `fid self blind` `sb` `fid maintenance proved` `mp` `fid registered` FALSE `fid includes spouse income` FALSE `fid exertion proved` FALSE `fid spouse income` 0 `fid allowance points` FALSE `fid spouse helped` FALSE `fid elects 39` FALSE

-- D070: resident, retirement age, maintenance proved: 1.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 37 for` (`fid s37 case` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS 1
-- D071: the spouse has reached retirement age: 1.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 37 for` (`fid s37 case` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS 1
-- D072: blind within s 9(5)(a): 1.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 37 for` (`fid s37 case` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS 1
-- D073: not a beneficiary individual: 0.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 37 for` (`fid s37 case` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS 0
-- D074: not resident: 0.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 37 for` (`fid s37 case` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS 0
-- D075: maintenance not proved: 0.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 37 for` (`fid s37 case` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS 0
-- D076: married but living apart, so no "בן זוג": 0.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 37 for` (`fid s37 case` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS 0

-- s 38: a resident registered spouse, joint computation, the spouse's income from work proved.
GIVEN `resident`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `registered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `includes`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `income`     IS A NUMBER
      `allowance`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 37 to 39`
`fid s38 case: resident` `resident` `fid s38 registered` `registered` `fid s38 includes` `includes` `fid s38 spouse income` `income` `fid s38 allowance` `allowance` `fid s38 retired` `beneficiary` MEANS
    `fid spouse case: resident` `resident` `fid has spouse` TRUE `fid self retired` `beneficiary` `fid spouse retired` FALSE `fid self blind` FALSE `fid maintenance proved` FALSE `fid registered` `registered` `fid includes spouse income` `includes` `fid exertion proved` TRUE `fid spouse income` `income` `fid allowance points` `allowance` `fid spouse helped` FALSE `fid elects 39` FALSE

-- D080: spouse's employment income 60,000, no s 40(a) points: 1.75.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 38 for` (`fid s38 case: resident` TRUE `fid s38 registered` TRUE `fid s38 includes` TRUE `fid s38 spouse income` 60000 `fid s38 allowance` FALSE `fid s38 retired` FALSE) `at a credit-point value of` `fid credit point value` EQUALS 1.75
-- D081: entitled to s 40(a) points: 2.0.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 38 for` (`fid s38 case: resident` TRUE `fid s38 registered` TRUE `fid s38 includes` TRUE `fid s38 spouse income` 60000 `fid s38 allowance` TRUE `fid s38 retired` FALSE) `at a credit-point value of` `fid credit point value` EQUALS 2
-- D082: and a beneficiary individual: 2.75.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 38 for` (`fid s38 case: resident` TRUE `fid s38 registered` TRUE `fid s38 includes` TRUE `fid s38 spouse income` 60000 `fid s38 allowance` FALSE `fid s38 retired` TRUE) `at a credit-point value of` `fid credit point value` EQUALS 2.75
-- D086: the claimant is the non-registered spouse: 0.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 38 for` (`fid s38 case: resident` TRUE `fid s38 registered` FALSE `fid s38 includes` TRUE `fid s38 spouse income` 60000 `fid s38 allowance` FALSE `fid s38 retired` FALSE) `at a credit-point value of` `fid credit point value` EQUALS 0
-- D087: registered spouse not resident: 0.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 38 for` (`fid s38 case: resident` FALSE `fid s38 registered` TRUE `fid s38 includes` TRUE `fid s38 spouse income` 60000 `fid s38 allowance` FALSE `fid s38 retired` FALSE) `at a credit-point value of` `fid credit point value` EQUALS 0
-- D088: separate computation, the spouse's income not included: 0.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 38 for` (`fid s38 case: resident` TRUE `fid s38 registered` TRUE `fid s38 includes` FALSE `fid s38 spouse income` 60000 `fid s38 allowance` FALSE `fid s38 retired` FALSE) `at a credit-point value of` `fid credit point value` EQUALS 0
-- D089: s 38(b), threshold 25,410; income 25,410: 0.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 38 for` (`fid s38 case: resident` TRUE `fid s38 registered` TRUE `fid s38 includes` TRUE `fid s38 spouse income` 25410 `fid s38 allowance` FALSE `fid s38 retired` FALSE) `at a credit-point value of` `fid credit point value` EQUALS 0
-- D090: income 25,411: 1.75.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 38 for` (`fid s38 case: resident` TRUE `fid s38 registered` TRUE `fid s38 includes` TRUE `fid s38 spouse income` 25411 `fid s38 allowance` FALSE `fid s38 retired` FALSE) `at a credit-point value of` `fid credit point value` EQUALS 1.75
-- D091: entitled to s 40(a), threshold 29,040: 29,040 gives 0, 29,041 gives 2.0.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 38 for` (`fid s38 case: resident` TRUE `fid s38 registered` TRUE `fid s38 includes` TRUE `fid s38 spouse income` 29040 `fid s38 allowance` TRUE `fid s38 retired` FALSE) `at a credit-point value of` `fid credit point value` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 38 for` (`fid s38 case: resident` TRUE `fid s38 registered` TRUE `fid s38 includes` TRUE `fid s38 spouse income` 29041 `fid s38 allowance` TRUE `fid s38 retired` FALSE) `at a credit-point value of` `fid credit point value` EQUALS 2
-- D093: for a beneficiary individual the s 37 point does not enter "חלקי נקודות הזיכוי" (my reading;
-- a recorded fork is also acceptable): the threshold stays 5 x 1.75 x 2,904 = 25,410.
#ASSERT `s 38(b) — five times the amount of the said parts of credit points, for` (`fid s38 case: resident` TRUE `fid s38 registered` TRUE `fid s38 includes` TRUE `fid s38 spouse income` 60000 `fid s38 allowance` FALSE `fid s38 retired` TRUE) `at a credit-point value of` `fid credit point value` EQUALS 25410

-- s 39: a resident whose spouse helped in his business.
GIVEN `resident`    IS A BOOLEAN
      `allowance`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 37 to 39`
`fid s39 case: resident` `resident` `fid s39 allowance` `allowance` `fid s39 retired` `beneficiary` MEANS
    `fid spouse case: resident` `resident` `fid has spouse` TRUE `fid self retired` `beneficiary` `fid spouse retired` FALSE `fid self blind` FALSE `fid maintenance proved` FALSE `fid registered` FALSE `fid includes spouse income` FALSE `fid exertion proved` FALSE `fid spouse income` 0 `fid allowance points` `allowance` `fid spouse helped` TRUE `fid elects 39` FALSE

-- D100: not entitled to s 40(a): 1.5.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 39 for` (`fid s39 case: resident` TRUE `fid s39 allowance` FALSE `fid s39 retired` FALSE) `at a credit-point value of` `fid credit point value` EQUALS 1.5
-- D101: entitled to s 40(a): 1.75.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 39 for` (`fid s39 case: resident` TRUE `fid s39 allowance` TRUE `fid s39 retired` FALSE) `at a credit-point value of` `fid credit point value` EQUALS 1.75
-- D105: and a beneficiary individual: 2.5.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 39 for` (`fid s39 case: resident` TRUE `fid s39 allowance` FALSE `fid s39 retired` TRUE) `at a credit-point value of` `fid credit point value` EQUALS 2.5
-- D106: not resident: 0.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 39 for` (`fid s39 case: resident` FALSE `fid s39 allowance` FALSE `fid s39 retired` FALSE) `at a credit-point value of` `fid credit point value` EQUALS 0

-- Entitled under both s 38 and s 39 for the same spouse (not entitled to s 40(a)).
GIVEN `elects 39` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 37 to 39`
`fid both 38 and 39, electing 39:` `elects 39` MEANS
    `fid spouse case: resident` TRUE `fid has spouse` TRUE `fid self retired` FALSE `fid spouse retired` FALSE `fid self blind` FALSE `fid maintenance proved` FALSE `fid registered` TRUE `fid includes spouse income` TRUE `fid exertion proved` TRUE `fid spouse income` 60000 `fid allowance points` FALSE `fid spouse helped` TRUE `fid elects 39` `elects 39`

-- D107: chose s 38: s 38 1.75, s 39 0.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 38 after the election under section 39, for` (`fid both 38 and 39, electing 39:` FALSE) `at a credit-point value of` `fid credit point value` EQUALS 1.75
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 39 for` (`fid both 38 and 39, electing 39:` FALSE) `at a credit-point value of` `fid credit point value` EQUALS 0
-- D108: chose s 39: s 39 1.5, s 38 0.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 39 for` (`fid both 38 and 39, electing 39:` TRUE) `at a credit-point value of` `fid credit point value` EQUALS 1.5
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 38 after the election under section 39, for` (`fid both 38 and 39, electing 39:` TRUE) `at a credit-point value of` `fid credit point value` EQUALS 0
-- D110: never both: 1.75 choosing s 38, 1.5 choosing s 39.
#ASSERT `the credit points under sections 37, 38 and 39 for` (`fid both 38 and 39, electing 39:` FALSE) `at a credit-point value of` `fid credit point value` EQUALS 1.75
#ASSERT `the credit points under sections 37, 38 and 39 for` (`fid both 38 and 39, electing 39:` TRUE) `at a credit-point value of` `fid credit point value` EQUALS 1.5

§§ `G. Section 40(b)`

GIVEN `born`        IS A NUMBER
      `who`         IS A `Father or mother of the child, for section 40(b)`
      `maintained`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `with`        IS A BOOLEAN
      `died`        IS A BOOLEAN
      `unregistered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `elects`      IS A BOOLEAN
      `o resident`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `o has (1)`   IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A child, for section 40(b)`
`fid child born` `born` `fid parent asked is` `who` `fid maintained` `maintained` `fid with parent` `with` `fid other parent died` `died` `fid one parent unregistered` `unregistered` `fid mother elects` `elects` `fid other resident` `o resident` `fid other has (1)` `o has (1)` MEANS
    `A child, for section 40(b)` WITH
        `tax year of birth`                                                                IS `born`
        `the parent is`                                                                    IS `who`
        `the parent maintained the child`                                                  IS `maintained`
        `the child is with the parent`                                                     IS `with`
        `in a single-parent family`                                                        IS TRUE
        `the other parent died in or before the tax year`                                  IS `died`
        `registered in the population register without the details of one parent`          IS `unregistered`
        `the mother elects to count one birth-year credit point in the following tax year` IS `elects`
        `the other parent is an Israeli resident in the tax year`                          IS `o resident`
        `the other parent has credit points for the child under paragraph (1)`             IS `o has (1)`

-- A child living with and maintained by the mother asked about; the other parent not resident.
GIVEN `born` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A child, for section 40(b)`
`fid mother's child born` `born` MEANS
    `fid child born` `born` `fid parent asked is` `the mother of the child` `fid maintained` TRUE `fid with parent` TRUE `fid other parent died` FALSE `fid one parent unregistered` FALSE `fid mother elects` FALSE `fid other resident` FALSE `fid other has (1)` FALSE

GIVEN `the year`  IS A NUMBER
      `resident`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `single`    IS A BOOLEAN
      `s37`       IS A BOOLEAN
      `apart`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `share`     IS A NUMBER
      `kids`      IS A LIST OF `A child, for section 40(b)`
GIVETH A `A parent in a tax year, for section 40(b)`
`fid parent in` `the year` `fid parent resident` `resident` `fid single-parent family parent` `single` `fid s37 entitled` `s37` `fid living apart` `apart` `fid maintenance share` `share` `fid children` `kids` MEANS
    `A parent in a tax year, for section 40(b)` WITH
        `tax year`                                    IS `the year`
        `an Israeli resident in the tax year`         IS `resident`
        `a parent in a single-parent family`          IS `single`
        `entitled to a credit point under section 37` IS `s37`
        `living apart from the other parent`          IS `apart`
        `share of the children's maintenance expenses borne` IS `share`
        `a foreign worker`                            IS FALSE
        `children`                                    IS `kids`

-- A resident single parent in 2026, not entitled under s 37, not living apart.
GIVEN `kids` IS A LIST OF `A child, for section 40(b)`
GIVETH A `A parent in a tax year, for section 40(b)`
`fid single parent in 2026 with` `kids` MEANS
    `fid parent in` 2026 `fid parent resident` TRUE `fid single-parent family parent` TRUE `fid s37 entitled` FALSE `fid living apart` FALSE `fid maintenance share` 0 `fid children` `kids`

GIVEN p IS A `A parent in a tax year, for section 40(b)`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`fid para (1) points of` p MEANS (`the credit points under section 40(b) for` p)'s `under paragraph (1), with the election of (1A1)`

GIVEN p IS A `A parent in a tax year, for section 40(b)`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`fid para (1A) points of` p MEANS (`the credit points under section 40(b) for` p)'s `under paragraph (1A), with the election of (1A1), against the tax on income from personal exertion`

GIVEN p IS A `A parent in a tax year, for section 40(b)`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`fid para (2) points of` p MEANS (`the credit points under section 40(b) for` p)'s `under paragraph (2)`

GIVEN p IS A `A parent in a tax year, for section 40(b)`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`fid all s 40(b) points of` p MEANS
         (`the credit points under section 40(b) for` p)'s `under paragraph (1), with the election of (1A1)`
    PLUS (`the credit points under section 40(b) for` p)'s `under paragraph (1A), with the election of (1A1), against the tax on income from personal exertion`
    PLUS (`the credit points under section 40(b) for` p)'s `under paragraph (1B), against the tax on income from personal exertion`
    PLUS (`the credit points under section 40(b) for` p)'s `under paragraph (2)`

