§§ `J. Section 64B`

GIVEN `first`  IS A NUMBER
      `second` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A couple, for section 64B`
`fid couple in 2026 with 2024 incomes` `first` `fid and` `second` MEANS
    `A couple, for section 64B` WITH
        `the first tax year in question`                             IS 2026
        `the first spouse's taxable income two tax years before it`  IS `first`
        `the second spouse's taxable income two tax years before it` IS `second`

-- D260: A 120,000, B 80,000: the officer may designate A, and only A.
#ASSERT `s 64B(a) — the assessing officer may determine that` `the first spouse` `is the registered spouse of` (`fid couple in 2026 with 2024 incomes` 120000 `fid and` 80000)
#ASSERT NOT `s 64B(a) — the assessing officer may determine that` `the second spouse` `is the registered spouse of` (`fid couple in 2026 with 2024 incomes` 120000 `fid and` 80000)
-- D261: A 100,001, B 99,999: A.
#ASSERT `s 64B(a) — the assessing officer may determine that` `the first spouse` `is the registered spouse of` (`fid couple in 2026 with 2024 incomes` 100001 `fid and` 99999)
-- D262: 100,000 each: (a) does not apply to either, and (c) does not apply (the designation itself is
-- refused, which no exported rule answers).
#ASSERT NOT `s 64B(a) — the assessing officer may determine that` `the first spouse` `is the registered spouse of` (`fid couple in 2026 with 2024 incomes` 100000 `fid and` 100000)
#ASSERT NOT `s 64B(a) — the assessing officer may determine that` `the second spouse` `is the registered spouse of` (`fid couple in 2026 with 2024 incomes` 100000 `fid and` 100000)
#ASSERT NOT `s 64B(c) — neither spouse had taxable income two tax years before, so the assessing officer may determine either, for` (`fid couple in 2026 with 2024 incomes` 100000 `fid and` 100000)
-- D263: neither had taxable income: the officer may designate either (c).
#ASSERT `s 64B(c) — neither spouse had taxable income two tax years before, so the assessing officer may determine either, for` (`fid couple in 2026 with 2024 incomes` 0 `fid and` 0)

GIVEN `jointly`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `day`      IS A DATE
      `first`    IS A NUMBER
      `elected`  IS A NUMBER
      `other`    IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An election of the registered spouse, for section 64B(b)`
`fid election: jointly` `jointly` `fid notified on` `day` `fid for tax year` `first` `fid elected spouse's income` `elected` `fid other's income` `other` MEANS
    `An election of the registered spouse, for section 64B(b)` WITH
        `the spouse elected to be registered`                         IS `the second spouse`
        `made jointly and in writing by both spouses`                 IS `jointly`
        `the day the notice was given`                                IS `day`
        `the first tax year it is to govern`                          IS `first`
        `that spouse's income in the tax year before the notice year` IS `elected`
        `the other spouse's income in the tax year before the notice year` IS `other`

-- D264: election for 2027 notified 2026-10-01: in time.
#ASSERT `s 64B(b) — the election is one the couple may make:` (`fid election: jointly` TRUE `fid notified on` (YMD 2026 10 1) `fid for tax year` 2027 `fid elected spouse's income` 50000 `fid other's income` 100000)
-- D265: notified 2026-10-02: late for 2027.
#ASSERT NOT `s 64B(b) — the election is one the couple may make:` (`fid election: jointly` TRUE `fid notified on` (YMD 2026 10 2) `fid for tax year` 2027 `fid elected spouse's income` 50000 `fid other's income` 100000)
-- D266: 2025 income B 25,000, A 100,000: exactly 25%, met.
#ASSERT `s 64B(b) — the election is one the couple may make:` (`fid election: jointly` TRUE `fid notified on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `fid for tax year` 2027 `fid elected spouse's income` 25000 `fid other's income` 100000)
-- D267: B 24,999: not met.
#ASSERT NOT `s 64B(b) — the election is one the couple may make:` (`fid election: jointly` TRUE `fid notified on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `fid for tax year` 2027 `fid elected spouse's income` 24999 `fid other's income` 100000)
-- D268: notice by one spouse alone: not an election.
#ASSERT NOT `s 64B(b) — the election is one the couple may make:` (`fid election: jointly` FALSE `fid notified on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `fid for tax year` 2027 `fid elected spouse's income` 50000 `fid other's income` 100000)
-- D269: a determination effective 2023 still stands in 2026 (no fresh (a) determination).
#ASSERT `s 64B(d)(1) — a determination or election first governing tax year` 2023 `still stands, unless they cease to be spouses or the Director decides, in tax year` 2026
-- D270: in 2028 it no longer binds: a fresh determination is allowed.
#ASSERT NOT `s 64B(d)(1) — a determination or election first governing tax year` 2023 `still stands, unless they cease to be spouses or the Director decides, in tax year` 2028
-- D272: an election of the other spouse for 2026, in time, 25% met: allowed.
#ASSERT `s 64B(b) — the election is one the couple may make:` (`fid election: jointly` TRUE `fid notified on` (YMD 2025 9 1) `fid for tax year` 2026 `fid elected spouse's income` 40000 `fid other's income` 100000)
-- D274: elected spouse's 2026 income 20,000 against 100,000: the officer may determine.
#ASSERT `s 64B(d)(2) — the assessing officer may determine the registered spouse for the year, the elected spouse having income` 20000 `against` 100000
-- D275: 25,000 against 100,000: the power does not arise.
#ASSERT NOT `s 64B(d)(2) — the assessing officer may determine the registered spouse for the year, the elected spouse having income` 25000 `against` 100000

§§ `K. Section 65`

GIVEN `whose`    IS A `Whose income, for section 65`
      `kind`     IS A `A kind of income, for section 65`
      `excepted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `An item of a household's income, for section 65`
`fid household item of` `whose` `fid kind` `kind` `fid inherited or injury` `excepted` MEANS
    `An item of a household's income, for section 65` WITH
        `whose`          IS `whose`
        `kind`           IS `kind`
        `taxable amount` IS 5000
        `from assets received by inheritance, or originating in compensation or insurance money received for bodily injury` IS `excepted`

-- D280: B's employment income 100,000: A's income, in A's name.
#ASSERT `s 65 — the item is charged in the registered spouse's name:` (`fid household item of` `the other spouse's` `fid kind` `any other income` `fid inherited or injury` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 65 — the income charged in the registered spouse's name, for the couple` (`A couple in a tax year, for section 65` WITH `tax year` IS 2026, `married, living together and running a joint household` IS TRUE, `a separate calculation under section 66 governs some of the couple's income` IS FALSE) `, from` (LIST `An item of a household's income, for section 65` WITH `whose` IS `the other spouse's`, `kind` IS `any other income`, `taxable amount` IS 100000, `from assets received by inheritance, or originating in compensation or insurance money received for bodily injury` IS FALSE) EQUALS 100000
-- D281: A's child aged 16, interest: included.
#ASSERT `s 65 — the item is charged in the registered spouse's name:` (`fid household item of` (`a child's, of the registered spouse` OF 16) `fid kind` `interest, discount or linkage differences` `fid inherited or injury` FALSE)
-- D282: born 2009 (turns 17 in 2026), interest: included.
#ASSERT `s 65 — the item is charged in the registered spouse's name:` (`fid household item of` (`a child's, of the registered spouse` OF 17) `fid kind` `interest, discount or linkage differences` `fid inherited or injury` FALSE)
-- D283: born 2008 (turns 18 in 2026), interest: not included.
#ASSERT NOT `s 65 — the item is charged in the registered spouse's name:` (`fid household item of` (`a child's, of the registered spouse` OF 18) `fid kind` `interest, discount or linkage differences` `fid inherited or injury` FALSE)
-- D284: interest from an inherited asset: not included.
#ASSERT NOT `s 65 — the item is charged in the registered spouse's name:` (`fid household item of` (`a child's, of the registered spouse` OF 16) `fid kind` `interest, discount or linkage differences` `fid inherited or injury` TRUE)
-- D285: interest from compensation for bodily injury: not included.
#ASSERT NOT `s 65 — the item is charged in the registered spouse's name:` (`fid household item of` (`a child's, of the registered spouse` OF 16) `fid kind` `interest, discount or linkage differences` `fid inherited or injury` TRUE)
-- D286: a capital gain: included.
#ASSERT `s 65 — the item is charged in the registered spouse's name:` (`fid household item of` (`a child's, of the registered spouse` OF 16) `fid kind` `capital gain` `fid inherited or injury` FALSE)
-- D287-D289: employment income, rent, a dividend: not included.
#ASSERT NOT `s 65 — the item is charged in the registered spouse's name:` (`fid household item of` (`a child's, of the registered spouse` OF 16) `fid kind` `any other income` `fid inherited or injury` FALSE)
-- D290: linkage differentials: included.
#ASSERT `s 65 — the item is charged in the registered spouse's name:` (`fid household item of` (`a child's, of the registered spouse` OF 16) `fid kind` `interest, discount or linkage differences` `fid inherited or injury` FALSE)
-- D291: income passed through from a real-estate investment fund: included.
#ASSERT `s 65 — the item is charged in the registered spouse's name:` (`fid household item of` (`a child's, of the registered spouse` OF 16) `fid kind` `income passed on by a real estate investment trust as defined in section 64A2` `fid inherited or injury` FALSE)

